    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5aa7210_b5af4cf7",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Vpn.java",
        "patchSetId": 53
      },
      "lineNbr": 1914,
      "author": {
        "id": 1221725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-29T00:47:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "They\u0027re not exactly the same. SetingsVpn is anything that is run from the Settings app, and LegacyVpn is always a subset of SettingVpn. However, the IKEv2/IPsec VPN can also be configured and run via the Settings UI, so it has some overlap (but is not a subset of).\n\n(If this doesn\u0027t come out properly, copy/paste into a fixed-type font)\n+------------------+-------------------+\n|   Settings VPN   |   App-based VPN   |\n+------------------+-------------------+\n| LegacyVpn | PlatformVpn | VpnService |\n|           |  (Ikev2Vpn) |            |\n+-----------+-------------+------------+\n\nLegacyVpn has external processes that it has to monitor, and as such it requires some additional locking and hackery to make sure that it works properly. Since the new Platform VPNs don\u0027t have those limitations, this is used to prevent unnecessary locking.",
      "parentUuid": "2d153dc4_13b63462",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1914,
        "startChar": 40,
        "endLine": 1914,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "62a4700ad0c4d4865a63ef6ed88cf8f702b1229c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
